## Verification complete — playable FPS on port 3000

**Summary:** Confirmed playable HTML entrypoint at \`./index.html\` (148 lines, ThreeJS 0.185.1 via CDN). App server running in tmux session \`app-server\` on port 3000 (\`python3 -m http.server 3000\`), serving \`index.html\` with HTTP 200. Gameplay: pointer-lock look, WASD, hitscan rifle with recoil/spread, wave bots with chase AI, HUD (HP/ammo/wave/kills), procedural WebAudio. Fixed dim lighting (hemi 0.9->1.4, sun 1.6->2.4) and re-verified after the fix that \`index.html\` is the page served.

**Public game link:** no public preview deployed in this environment; run locally: \`python3 -m http.server 3000\` then open http://localhost:3000/ (verified). Source: https://github.com/AgentsLoop/PlayGround/blob/${SHA}/index.html

**Final commit:** https://github.com/AgentsLoop/PlayGround/commit/${SHA}

**Deployment and test status:**
- tmux \`app-server\` on :3000: RUNNING, serves ./index.html (HTTP 200).
- Browser test (chromium headless + SwiftShader, 1280x720, virtual-time 8s): PASS — page renders, overlay + HUD + 3D arena + enemy bots visible, no fatal JS errors.
- JS syntax check (\`node --check\` on inline module): PASS.
- Re-checked \`index.html\` exists after every fix: PASS.

**Known limitations:** Greybox systems demo, openly not Call of Duty visual parity — procedural boxes only, no scanned PBR, no GI/volumetrics, no mocap, no multiplayer/netcode. Full AAA parity is blocked (needs studio-scale assets/team/budget).

